=== Verdict ===

  STRUCTURAL-LIMIT — the current discovery kinds saturate at L4
  on substrates of OQ#1's family. L5 = 0 because only 1 L4 super-meta
  exists per substrate; you need ≥ 2 L4s sharing an L3 to mint L5.

  To lift the ceiling, one of the following is required:
    (a) more diverse premise / conclusion shapes → more L2 → more L3 → more L4
    (b) additional L2/L3 discovery kinds (e.g., shared-variable-arity,
        shared-symmetry, shared-conclusion-orientation)
    (c) multi-substrate aggregation: combine multiple substrate runs and
        discover families across the union (not yet implemented)

  This finding parallels C.2.1's verdict (OQ#2 yielded 0 axioms because
  the substrate violated transitivity — structural bound, not bug).

  L4 is the deepest layer the current vocabulary supports. Further
  abstraction needs new discovery kinds, not bigger substrates.

